The roller keeps itself: troves/kiosk-screen, kept by bay 1's pool pass

Editing bay 1 drives the rolling TV the way kiosk-1 keeps its panels: Edge in
kiosk mode, fullscreen, a profile of its own, put back when it goes missing.
No service: the pool's five-minute task runs one `keep` per pass.

- [ ] troves/kiosk-screen/screen.ps1: status | keep | on | off | reset
  - find the instrument by EDID (instrument.yml `match:`), never the display number
  - no match: nothing shown, and our own browser closed if Windows piled it elsewhere
  - source: the depot's wall when 10.209.1.1:445 answers, else a local render
    of the wall from the mirror's door.py (Autumn, 2026-09-27)
  - stop by the pid it started, never by name (GRANTS)
- [ ] troves/kiosk-screen/render.py: wall_files() to the trove's prefix, whole or not at all
- [ ] pool.ps1 pass calls `keep roller-tv`
- [ ] fcpm screen [status|on|off|reset]
- [ ] follow it on the roller: keep, close by hand, keep, off, on, unplug-shaped (no match)
- [ ] READMEs: troves table, instruments, editing-bay-1 PROFILE

Open: the local render has no bookings (the M365 key is kiosk-1's) and no depot
files, so Studio shows the map without appointments and Files is empty.
